Charanti—They wander; Hi—Indeed; Avanau—On earth; Kamam—According to desire; Brahmanaah—Brahmins; Bhagavat-
Priyah—Extremely dear to Shri Bhagavan, even Vaishnavas; Ma-drisham—Like me; Gramya-buddhinam—Afflicted by momentary material consciousness; Bodhaya—To preach; Unmatta-linginah—Wearing the guise of a madman. The most beloved servant of Shri Krishna, the Brahmin, who has attained the status of a Vaishnava, sometimes
sometimes disguises himself as an Avadhuta and, like us materialists, who are always engrossed in sensual pleasure,
to benefit them and to remove their ignorance, they keep wandering on the earth according to their
wishes. Kumaro Narada Ribhurangira Devaloositha.
