There are many cunning gurus who show magic to their disciples, and there are many foolish disciples who
like to see such magic for material gain. Such disciples, in order to escape the darkness of ignorance,
have no interest in leading a spiritual life. It is said—

Om, the one who is blinded by the darkness of ignorance, with the lotus of knowledge and the flame of knowledge. Salutations to that Guru, by whom the eyes are opened. “I was born in the deep darkness of ignorance, and my guru opened my eyes with the lamp of knowledge.
I opened my eyes. I greet them." From this, the definition of a guru is obtained. Every person
is in the darkness of ignorance, therefore everyone needs to be illuminated by divine knowledge. The true guru is the one who, by providing light to his disciple, liberates him from the deep darkness of this world caused by ignorance. Shriangira said:
I am the son of that son, O king.
This is the son of Brahma, the direct Narada, the sage. 17). Meaning of the word.

