Was. In fact, I am the same Angira Rishi who gave you this son. These that you have,
are the direct sons of Lord Brahma, the great sage Narada. Thus, immersed in the sorrow of his son, he is in distress. Atadrhyamanusmrtam mahapurushagocaram. 18>. I have come here for your grace, O Lord. Brahmano bhagavatbhakto navaasaditumarhasi. 19.

He came to preach to him so that he could be saved from this ignorance. Another important word
is Brahman. Sometimes, in the prayer to God, he is addressed as 'Namo Brahmanya-Devaya,'
which means 'Salutations to God' because devotees serve Him. Therefore, this verse
tells—Brahmanas, devotees of the Lord, or those who are not worthy of being praised. This is the characteristic of a supreme devotee. Brahmabhutah prasannatma. A supreme devotee and a self-realized devotee have no reason to be happy or sad.
No. He is always beyond the bounds of mortal life. I grant that knowledge to those who come to my home. I give you my son, who is the knower of the truth. 20. Meaning of the word

